  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ma&#x2019;an Aqwa (Stronger Together): Addressing Conflict and Climate Change for Durable Peace in Darfur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catholic Relief Services (CRS), together with the Catholic Agency for Overseas Development (CAFOD) and local implementing partners West Darfur Youth Organization for Development (WDYOD) and Kebkabyia Small Holders Charitable Society (KCS), propose to implement Ma&#x2019;an Aqwa (Stronger Together) to mitigate conflict resulting from climate change and enhance climate change adaptation and mitigation measures in West and North Darfur states. CRS has been working at the nexus of conflict and climate in the Darfur region since 2004.Based on this analysis and engagement, CRS and its co-applicants designed Ma&#x2019;an Aqwa to achieve: 
Overall objective: Conflict resulting from climate change mitigated and climate change adaptation/mitigation measures enhanced in West and North Darfur states
Specific objective (SOs):  
1.	Governance structures at local, national and regional levels to address risks that are both conflict and climate related strengthened 
2.	Local communities&#x2019; resilience to better respond to and cope with climate change and conflict strengthened
3.	Communication and collaboration across communities and disciplines, from climate science and natural resource management experts to peacebuilding and development actors improved</narrative>
  </description>
